    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101480" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύστομ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with a narrow mouth</i>,
			opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεγαλόστομος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				662a24
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); of a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέτοικος</span> (called
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάφη</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
				-ώτερος σκάφης</span>, prov. of one whose low birth makes
			him keep silence, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				191
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				103
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ς. τῶν τευχέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archyt.
					1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πίθος μέγας καὶ ς</span>.
				Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.392
			</span></i> P., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Spir.</u>
				1
			</span></i>
			<u>Praef.</u>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>mouth to mouth</i>, of a kiss, <i><span class="en">
				Telecl.
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
